Subject: do not abort when a fake-root process calls chroot

Under --root-id, chroot(2) is emulated by replacing the tracee's file system
namespace (tracee->fs) with one rooted at the new directory. The old
namespace is freed at that point, and its lists of bindings are destroyed by
remove_bindings(), which found "its" tracee as the grandparent of the list
(talloc_parent twice). A namespace being freed is already detached from the
tracee, so the lookup hit NULL and talloc aborted:

    ./path/binding.c:438: Type mismatch: name[NULL] expected[Tracee]

and every process of the container died. The macro also unlinked from
tracee->fs, which after the swap is the *new* namespace. Any program that
calls chroot() while it is fake root triggers it: OpenSSH's privilege
separation (sshd), debootstrap-style scripts. It is present in the pinned
termux/proot and in the series up to 0015.

remove_bindings() now uses the list's own parent, the FileSystemNameSpace
that owns it, for both the lookup and the unlinking.

Upstream: termux/proot @ 7266fb3e8516535682f5a9c8f3a7e70f6506eddb (v5.1.107.92), after patches 0001-0015

diff --git a/src/path/binding.c b/src/path/binding.c
index 12d6505..ba6088f 100644
--- a/src/path/binding.c
+++ b/src/path/binding.c
@@ -422,25 +422,33 @@ Binding *insort_binding3(const Tracee *tracee, const TALLOC_CTX *context,
 static int remove_bindings(Bindings *bindings)
 {
 	Binding *binding;
-	Tracee *tracee;
+	FileSystemNameSpace *fs;
+
+	/* The namespace owning this list, not "the tracee's current one": a
+	 * chroot(2) replaces tracee->fs and frees the old namespace, whose
+	 * lists are then destroyed while it is already detached from the
+	 * tracee.  */
+	fs = talloc_get_type_abort(talloc_parent(bindings), FileSystemNameSpace);
 
 	/* Unlink all bindings from the @link list.  */
 #define CIRCLEQ_REMOVE_ALL(name) do {				\
 	binding = CIRCLEQ_FIRST(bindings);			\
 	while (binding != (void *) bindings) {			\
 		Binding *next = CIRCLEQ_NEXT(binding, link.name);\
-		CIRCLEQ_REMOVE_(tracee, binding, name);		\
+		CIRCLEQ_REMOVE(fs->bindings.name, binding, link.name);\
+		binding->link.name.cqe_next = NULL;		\
+		binding->link.name.cqe_prev = NULL;		\
+		talloc_unlink(fs->bindings.name, binding);	\
 		binding = next;					\
 	}							\
 } while (0)
 
 	/* Search which link is used by this list.  */
-	tracee = TRACEE(bindings);
-	if (bindings == tracee->fs->bindings.pending)
+	if (bindings == fs->bindings.pending)
 		CIRCLEQ_REMOVE_ALL(pending);
-	else if (bindings == tracee->fs->bindings.guest)
+	else if (bindings == fs->bindings.guest)
 		CIRCLEQ_REMOVE_ALL(guest);
-	else if (bindings == tracee->fs->bindings.host)
+	else if (bindings == fs->bindings.host)
 		CIRCLEQ_REMOVE_ALL(host);
 
 	bzero(bindings, sizeof(Bindings));
